course: dictionary
lesson: 2023
title: Confidence: feeling sure and trusting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confidence is the feeling that you can do something well, and that you believe in yourself. «She answered with confidence.» The word with tells you how she answered: she was sure, not nervous. Try it: swap in sure and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Confidence can also mean trust in someone or something. «Confident writing makes people trust it, but confidence is not proof.» The writing sounds sure, so people trust it, but sounding sure does not make it true. Confidence feels good, but it still needs checking.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «Dancing in a group first can build the confidence to dance alone.» Build tells you confidence can grow bit by bit, the way a wall is built. Practising and trying again help it grow.
fact: Confidence means the feeling that you can do something well, or belief in yourself.
fact: Confidence in someone or something means trust that they are good or will work well.
fact: A confidence is a secret you tell someone you trust, as in «in confidence».
fact: Confidence grows through practice, making mistakes and trying again.
fact: Confidence is not proof: a person can sound sure and still be wrong.
exercise: «She answered with confidence.» What does confidence mean here? | Losing her voice | Hiding under the desk | Being cross with the teacher | *Being sure of herself
exercise: «Confident writing makes people trust it, but confidence is not proof.» What does this sentence teach you? | Confident writing is always right | Writers should never be sure of anything | Proof is the same thing as confidence | *Looking sure does not make something true
exercise: A friend tells you a secret «in confidence». What does this mean? | It is a secret that everyone already knows | You must shout it out to the class | *It is meant to stay private, but a secret about someone being hurt must go to a trusted adult | It is a secret about the weather
test: «Dancing in a group first can build the confidence to dance alone.» What helps confidence grow in this sentence? | Forgetting all the steps | Sitting still at the side | Never trying at all | *Dancing in a group first
test: «There are free children's helplines with trained people who listen in confidence.» What does listen in confidence mean? | They will only listen if you are older | They cannot hear you on the phone | *They listen privately and will help you | They will tell everyone at school
exam: Which statement about confidence is true? | Confidence can only come from being born that way | Being confident means you never make mistakes | *Feeling sure does not prove that you are right | Confident people never need to practise
